$$\\begin{cases} 6x - 9y = 14 \\\\ kx + 12y = -5 \\end{cases}$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$-18$"},{"key":"B","text":"$8$"},{"key":"C","text":"$18$"},{"key":"D","text":"$-8$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'D', NULL, E'A system has no solution when the lines are parallel — same slope but different $y$-intercepts. Rewriting the first equation in slope-intercept form: $y = \\frac{6}{9}x - \\frac{14}{9} = \\frac{2}{3}x - \\frac{14}{9}$. The slope is $\\frac{2}{3}$. For the second equation: $y = -\\frac{k}{12}x - \\frac{5}{12}$. Setting slopes equal: $-\\frac{k}{12} = \\frac{2}{3}$, so $k = -8$. The intercepts $-\\frac{14}{9}$ and $-\\frac{5}{12}$ are indeed different, confirming no solution. The distractor $8$ results from dropping the negative sign when solving $-\\frac{k}{12} = \\frac{2}{3}$. The distractor $18$ comes from finding the value that makes the slopes negative reciprocals (perpendicular lines), confusing the condition for no solution with perpendicularity. The distractor $-18$ combines both errors — applying the perpendicularity condition and then also introducing a sign error.', $lyceon_json${"D":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 90, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);







What is the value of $y$ in the solution to the system of equations above?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, '2', ARRAY['2'], E'From the second equation, $x = y + 3$. Substituting into the first equation: $3(y + 3) + 2y = 19$, which simplifies to $3y + 9 + 2y = 19$, then $5y = 10$, so $y = 2$. A common error is solving for $x$ instead: substituting back gives $x = 5$, but the question asks for $y$. Another error is subtracting $9$ incorrectly or distributing the $3$ only to $y$ and not to $3$.', NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 60, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);





























